            <ArticleTitle>Bilateral lower limb compartment syndrome: a potentially destructive complication of breast reduction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e155-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1308/003588412X13171221589379</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Compartment syndrome is a serious condition in which the pressure in the limb increases and potentially compromises capillary circulation with subsequent ischaemic complications. This case report presents a case of bilateral lower limb compartment syndrome after bilateral breast reduction for back pain. The patient was an otherwise healthy 24-year-old Afro-Caribbean woman. This report aims to highlight the need for an increased index of suspicion for compartment syndrome in any postoperative patient complaining of lower limb pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
